(7753479, 1281382, 1031, '<td valign="top"><a href="//oedilf.com/db/Lim.php?Word=AFLAC" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">AFLAC</a> by <a href="//www.oedilf.com/db/Lim.php?AuthorId=405" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">GeneralE</a> <br/> <br/><b>A</b>ghast, I just stared at the screen.<br/><b>F</b>orgive me, but what does this mean?<br/><b>L</b>ike, some duck talking to<br/><b>A</b>ll these guys with no clue<br/><b>C</b>ould convince me insurance is keen!<br/> <br/><b>AFLAC</b> is the American Family Life Assurance Company of Columbus, Ohio, which has run a TV ad campaign featuring people oblivious to the duck offering them insurance advice. Since initiating the ads in 1999, the company''s name-recognition (in nationwide polling) has risen from 10 to 90 percent, so perhaps not <i>everyone</i> has remained oblivious.</td>', 'AFLAC by GeneralE  Aghast, I just stared at the screen.Forgive me, but what does this mean?Like, some duck talking toAll these guys with no clueCould convince me insurance is keen! AFLAC is the American Family Life Assurance Company of Columbus, Ohio, which has run a TV ad campaign featuring people oblivious to the duck offering them insurance advice. Since initiating the ads in 1999, the company''s name-recognition (in nationwide polling) has risen from 10 to 90 percent, so perhaps not everyone has remained oblivious.', '2023-07-07 20:57:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(7753481, 1281382, 96751, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GeneralE:</b></div><hr/><i> <a href="//oedilf.com/db/Lim.php?Word=AFLAC" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">AFLAC</a> by <a href="//www.oedilf.com/db/Lim.php?AuthorId=405" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">GeneralE</a> <br/> <br/><b>A</b>ghast, I just stared at the screen.<br/><b>F</b>orgive me, but what does this mean?<br/><b>L</b>ike, some duck talking to<br/><b>A</b>ll these guys with no clue<br/><b>C</b>ould convince me insurance is keen!<br/> <br/><b>AFLAC</b> is the American Family Life Assurance Company of Columbus, Ohio, which has run a TV ad campaign featuring people oblivious to the duck offering them insurance advice. Since initiating the ads in 1999, the company''s name-recognition (in nationwide polling) has risen from 10 to 90 percent, so perhaps not <i>everyone</i> has remained oblivious. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL!<br/>That''s AWESOME, Paul</td>', 'Originally posted by GeneralE: AFLAC by GeneralE  Aghast, I just stared at the screen.Forgive me, but what does this mean?Like, some duck talking toAll these guys with no clueCould convince me insurance is keen! AFLAC is the American Family Life Assurance Company of Columbus, Ohio, which has run a TV ad campaign featuring people oblivious to the duck offering them insurance advice. Since initiating the ads in 1999, the company''s name-recognition (in nationwide polling) has risen from 10 to 90 percent, so perhaps not everyone has remained oblivious.   LOL!That''s AWESOME, Paul', '2023-07-07 21:15:03.000000', NULL, 0);
